[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known with one fix queued. The reports in it describe three
different problems, and the queued parser fix closes only the first.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket; #4471 stays open until all three close.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get the day and
  month swapped, through every channel except booking-v3's form.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, people type month first as
  told, and the form reads the tenant's day-first way. Same symptom, different code. The parser fix
  does not touch it.
- **`one-day`**: the date lands one day early, or on different days for people in different
  zones (Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday). Nothing is swapped. These are the reports the
  desk already read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`), which the cause table still counts as `parser`.

## How the reports were placed

Every report merged into #4471 was read, once per id: the export repeats some reports across its
overlapping pages. The problem comes from the tenant's locale and booking form (`causes.ts`) and the
desk's reading of the body, never from intake's tag, which is a guess from the reporter's browser.
The last column counts reports intake tagged with a different cause.

For comparison, the cause table on #4471, which knows only two causes:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What this changes for the desk

- Subject lines do not separate these problems: several subjects turn up in all three. Read the
  tenant and the channel before you merge.
- Ship the parser fix and #4471 still gets reports from booking-v3's form and one-day moves. Route
  those to their own tickets.

